      "side": 1,
      "message": "Most usages I found are actually setting the attribute `value` instead of the proprety.\n\nThen to fetch you can do `getAttribute(value)` instead of `.value`.\n\nSo specifically\n\n```\nmd-outlined-select\n        id\u003d\"labelMin\"\n        value\u003d${convertToString(this.rule?.value?.min)}\n        ?disabled\u003d${!this.editing}\n        @change\u003d${this.handleMinChange}\n      \u003e\n```\n\nThen in the test you should do \n\n```\nqueryAndAssert(element,\u0027#force\u0027).getAttribute(\u0027value\u0027)\n```",
